     This is correct.  Save and bones files older than the executable
program will be rejected.  Most if not all the "Install.*" files warn
that old save and bones files should be discarded.

> altho this doesn't help you now, pl9 bones/saves are compatible with
> pl10.  however, you do have to update the timestamp of those files.
> on Unix that's "touch bones* save/*" or something similar ...

     No, patchlevel 10's format is completely incompatable with
earlier versions, except perhaps for the Macintosh and Amiga ports,
which use different save & restore code.  For Unix, VMS, DOS, OS/2,
and Atari, there's 0% chance of successfully using pl9 save or bones
files with pl10.  The object save & restore code has been revised
(some may say broken :-).

